  "details": "The upcoming VRCPlayerApi.AttachTransformToBone is great! It would be nice though to attach to more things on players than just humanoid bones.\n\nFor example, any of the tracking points: Origin, AvatarRoot, Head, LeftHand, RightHand. For example, attaching to Hand tracking points would be great for holding weapons in game worlds where you shouldn't ever drop the weapon. I already know of worlds that do that.\n\nAlso, attaching to the point returned by GetPosition(), which is a little different than all the tracking points. (Which I think is the position of the player capsule??? Maybe???)\n\nI could imagine this API:\n\n    AttachTransformToBone\n\n    AttachTransformToTrackingPoint\n\n    AttachTransformToCapsule   (attaches to GetPosition()/GetRotation())\n\n    DetachTransform\n\nI'm suggesting this now while the AttachTransform feature is still in beta, because the current function name \"DetachTransformFromBone\" is limiting. A more generic \"DetachTransform\" name will allow for expansion to more attachment points in the future without needing to make more Detach functions.",
